<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:33Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:838d0256d26b85dab86f4f07dfd2e1f2169da0120539fcd15cc74e9b2413b381</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89cacca9b340244bac27a114b3ab5b8734187b6eaa1891bc6dfae64d2e088aee</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi Jinping renews calls for 'reunification' with Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8c6edddacfcbda402c1e99df4d50fae88a32ab3d2be9f61619204234503655e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738--c3c1f561b896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping said that reunification was inevitable, but stopped short of mentioning military force. Taiwan though swiftly rejected Beijing's demands as tensions continue over the island's future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news : Modi government approves $340 million museum in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5f7e04294c3ce548bcddf7ef877c342488b01f77a2c2e174b4fccbf3dfda45e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477--8b8209e9e65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The government says that the 'Yuge Yugeen Bharat Museum' will have the world's "largest" museum dispaly area." DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a8976e7225d3cca5c2d1db4ad1b2e63dba1698c9759cf1b99b3ab8bd6e1184c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: CPCB addresses stark Delhi pollution data gap on Diwali night</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c2de22fdf3cfbdff359c4445192ec4d068985b16347e6bdfadc26350b65cdb</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cpcb-addresses-stark-delhi-pollution-data-gap-on-diwali-night/live-79914190--aefe747adc18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cpcb-addresses-stark-delhi-pollution-data-gap-on-diwali-night/live-79914190?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's main pollution monitor has issued a clarification on a wide air quality data gap between official and private reporting in New Delhi that saw the city choked amid Diwali fireworks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea bus causes large crash near Seoul, dozens hurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98209d9c8221f74282ead2cdf6a9e49beff9dd019ed08b78274bbdfc68aa8952</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T04:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-bus-causes-large-crash-near-seoul-dozens-hurt/a-79914074--7b0b10a102d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-bus-causes-large-crash-near-seoul-dozens-hurt/a-79914074?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bus triggered a collision involving more than 30 vehicles, including other buses, during rush hour traffic in the South Korean city of Seongnam, just south of Seoul.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Former Malaysian leader Najib Razak returns home under royal pardon, but faces a separate 15-year prison sentence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9b83f5ff2da0193272b790691b2640a1f9e7c608306ca79d0b13da3b763550a</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/former-malaysian-leader-najib-razak-returns-home-under-royal-pardon-but-faces-a-separate-15-year-pri/a-79913437--5df11bf7bdda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/former-malaysian-leader-najib-razak-returns-home-under-royal-pardon-but-faces-a-separate-15-year-prison-sentence/a-79913437?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Najib Razak has left prison under a royal pardon, prompting a minister to resign in protest. Malaysia's former leader still faces a separate 15-year sentence over the corruption scandal that brought him down.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a282a6c876382ac014fc4bb5de449ee3b62b5d644c064c7a484fe75f4bd809</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Japan watches for signs of change in Trump's foreign policy priorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c364d4d8b8341a3a462e678b0ab6e79691d0d9d7318364bd960445c0a788ae</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398--c0dcb3ef3493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tokyo fears the drubbing US President Donald Trump suffered in last week's midterm election may push him to pursue a diplomatic quick win at the expense of Washington's allies in the Indo-Pacific.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, economic benefits still disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dce68e99ebf9ea713ab693a8b88ea43d2a1b4e67651b0a14c66447fc41b5226</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331--2fc450e61f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13585655ca57fd0a73bc41af6a3cb21b46e7bd0376c12a288b6df7fbb5a73b2c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02cc59e70ebebd98bbea286f5220e6bfcd25278e40bf5bf3d48cc22e763eda</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>8 ways the US midterm election could affect Donald Trump's Iran policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32e88a8b9031df3fcd76a56a87501df645c286f38c6d0c75aa425b089fa4bb4</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816--8cf7f9243f7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the US midterms could open a window for diplomacy with Iran, they could also unleash a new military escalation. DW spoke with analysts to identify eight factors that could tip the balance toward war or peace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c897b1188dc56aa7635610b875c9a6ec585de865ac3bece95dbfaf201a41db</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3279be22e5c6655d8f26cb67f0f70830893102ef42aad04dae0645476771f4</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
